# Verible SystemVerilog formatter configuration for this project.
#
# Passed to verible-verilog-format via `--flagfile=verible.flags` from
# the top-level Makefile. These flags capture the style the RTL already
# follows: 4-space indentation, 100-column limit, aligned port /
# parameter / named-connection / assignment groups, and `end else` kept
# on one line (matching the existing `end else begin` idiom).
#
# Edit this file to change the project-wide formatting policy; do NOT
# pass overriding flags on the Makefile command line or the two will
# drift apart.

--indentation_spaces=4
--column_limit=100
--try_wrap_long_lines=true
--wrap_end_else_clauses=false

# Align repeated declarations / connections / assignments into columns
# (matches the existing hand-aligned port and always-block style).
--port_declarations_alignment=align
--named_port_alignment=align
--named_parameter_alignment=align
--assignment_statement_alignment=align